{"name":"Cyprus","hex":"#0f4645","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cyprus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An island and country in the Mediterranean Sea, normally considered politically part of Europe but geographically part of West Asia. Official name: Republic of Cyprus. Capital: Nicosia.","A suburban area of Beckton, borough of Newham, Greater London, England, named after the Mediterranean island ."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thin, translucent, usually black fabric, a kind of crape."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cyprus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cyprus","blocks":[{"text":"Cyprus, officially the Republic of Cyprus, is an island country in the eastern Mediterranean Sea, located off the coast of the Levant mainland in West Asia. The island of Cyprus, which is the third largest and third most populous island in the Mediterranean, is divided along the United Nations Buffer Zone between the internationally recognised Republic of Cyprus and the Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus, which is recognised only by Turkey. The south of the island also hosts the British sovereign military bases of Akrotiri and Dhekelia. The capital and largest city of Cyprus is Nicosia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Flag_of_Cyprus.svg/330px-Flag_of_Cyprus.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyprus"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Geology_of_Cyprus-SkiriotissaMine.jpg/500px-Geology_of_Cyprus-SkiriotissaMine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Geology_of_Cyprus-SkiriotissaMine.jpg/1280px-Geology_of_Cyprus-SkiriotissaMine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Geology_